<body>
    <h1>Domain Realm Mapping in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>With domain realm assignment, a host name is translated into the=
 corresponding Kerberos realm name. This article shows how to configure dom=
ain realm mapping in IGEL OS.</p>
<hr>
<p>Menu path: <strong>Security &gt; Active Directory/Kerberos &gt; Domain R=
ealm Mapping</strong></p>
<p></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper c=
onfluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image con=
fluence-content-image-border image-left" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=
=3D"d559b36ef3ea1fd5b43da0e89a612b1e79f1a24b52856c64abc6c5bed91186a3" data-=
image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/7330=
2307/OS12_Actived%20Kerberos_Domain%20Realm.png?version=3D1&amp;modificatio=
nDate=3D1716364680996&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"954=
" data-width=3D"1126" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resou=
rce-id=3D"73309230" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource=
-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"OS12_Actived Ker=
beros_Domain Realm.png" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wi=
ki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-co=
ntainer-id=3D"73302307" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"5" data-m=
edia-id=3D"30a22841-700b-4aab-a4c4-115d8b2e754e" data-media-type=3D"file" h=
eight=3D"396"></span>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Use default DNS domain - Active Directory domain mapping</strong=
></p>
<p>=E2=98=91&nbsp;The DNS name and Active Directory domain name match. (Def=
ault)</p>
<p>=E2=98=90&nbsp;DNS name and Active Directory domain name assignments mus=
t be set up.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Domain Realm Mapping</strong></p>
<p>To manage the list of realm mappings:</p>
<div class=3D"error">
<span class=3D"error">Unable to render {include}</span> The included page c=
ould not be found.
</div>
<p><br><br><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-blue3">To set up a DNS name to =
Active Directory domain name assignment proceed as follows:</span></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Click&nbsp;<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper"><img class=
=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-content-image-inline" alt=3D"image=
-20240716-105027.png" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"e450d6b5c5885aa7eb7901938ec5b=
142e1478d9f8713293538655ebb37d88b68" data-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.at=
lassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302307/image-20240716-105027.png?ve=
rsion=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1721127029293&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-height=3D"25" data-width=3D"27" data-unresolved-comment-count=
=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"121342078" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-defaul=
t-alias=3D"image-20240716-105027.png" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.at=
lassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-link=
ed-resource-container-id=3D"73302307" data-linked-resource-container-versio=
n=3D"5" data-media-id=3D"644459f1-de6a-43bc-b7c9-4be7e18c8cd1" data-media-t=
ype=3D"file" width=3D"27" height=3D"25"></span> &nbsp;to create a new entry=
.<br>
The Add dialog is displayed.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Under&nbsp;<strong>DNS host or domain name</strong>, enter the lower cas=
e FQDN name of a host or a domain that is to be assigned to an Active Direc=
tory domain name. Example: <code>.example.com</code><br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Under&nbsp;<strong>Active Directory domain name</strong>, enter the Acti=
ve Directory domain name that is to be assigned to the host name.<br></p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Click&nbsp;<strong>Confirm</strong>.<br>
The data entered will be added to the&nbsp;<strong>Domain Realm Mapping&nbs=
p;</strong>list.</p></li>
</ol>
    </div>
</body>
